gxde-kwin-x11 for Debian
------------------------

The runtime binary package is named gxde-kwin-x11-6 so that it does not replace
the existing GXDE 5.x package named gxde-kwin-x11. The fork's files are under
their own namespace and do not conflict with the existing KWin files.

Debian's libkdecorations3-6 package declares a Breaks against KDecoration 2,
so installing libkdecorations3-dev would remove GXDE's existing window manager.
This source therefore builds against gxde-decoration3-x11 (KDecoration 3 built
under a GXDE-specific library name, see libgxde-decoration3-x11-dev), which can
be installed next to the KDecoration 2 runtime. Decoration plugins built
against the distribution libkdecorations3, such as kwin-style-breeze, are not
compatible with this build.

Night Light likewise uses gxde-nighttime-x11 (libgxde-nighttime-x11-dev) instead
of KNightTime, which is not available for this distribution. Its scheduling
service is D-Bus activated as com.gxde.NightTimeX11. Building with the
pkg.gxde-kwin-x11.no-nightlight profile disables Night Light entirely.

The GXDE/Deepin window manager compatibility layer from gxde-wm-shim
(gxde-wm-shim/ in this source, see debian/copyright) is built into this
package, in this project's namespace so that it can coexist with the
gxde-wm-shim package of the existing window manager:

 - The com.deepin.wm service is gxde-kwin_x11-wm-dbus in libexec. It is not
   D-Bus activated: the gxdewmshim KWin plugin starts it in GXDE, Deepin and
   DDE sessions (XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP) and stops it together with KWin. Set
   GXDE_KWIN_X11_WM_SHIM=1 or =0 to force it on or off.
 - Its defaults are installed as /etc/xdg/gxde-kwin_x11rc and
   /etc/xdg/gxde-kwin_x11rulesrc. The shared kglobalshortcutsrc, klaunchrc and
   kdeglobals files are not installed, nor are deepin-kwin's DConfig
   descriptions or the kwin_no_scale wrapper.
 - The hot zone and shortcut scripts are ported to the KWin 6 scripting API.
   workspace.__dde__ only existed in deepin-kwin; the run command action uses
   the StartDetached method of the gxdewmshim plugin instead. The gtkframe
   script is not installed because KWin handles _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS itself.

The source still compiles shared Wayland protocol and support code used by the
KWin core library. This is not a Wayland compositor build: neither
kwin_wayland nor gxde-kwin_wayland is a CMake target or an installed file.

The package build disables upstream tests and screen-locker integration, then
explicitly enables only the gxde-kwin_x11 executable backend.
